---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LanguageToggle from '../../components/LanguageToggle.astro';
import SocialLinks from '../../components/SocialLinks.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const qrPath = `${base}qr/2026-09-06-altar-of-our-church.png`;
const pageURL = 'https://dmicalambacity.org/2026-09-06-altar-of-our-church/';
const logoPath = `${base}dmi-logo.jpg`;

const translations = {
  languageLabel: 'Wika',
  languageAriaLabel: 'Wika ng pagbabasa',
  navAria: 'Pangunahing navigation',
  homeAria: 'Bumalik sa DMI Calamba City home',
  summaryAria: 'Buod ng study',
  takeawayAria: 'Pangunahing takeaway ng study',
  qrLinkAria: 'Buksan ang Bible study na ito',
  qrImageAlt: 'QR code para sa The Altar of Our Church Bible study',
  eyebrow: 'Bible Study · Gawa 2:42–47',
  title: 'Ang Altar ng Ating Simbahan',
  subtitle: 'Ang Iglesyang Ninanais ng Diyos',
  heroScripture: '<sup>42</sup> Nanatili sila sa mga turo ng mga apostol, sa pagsasama-sama bilang magkakapatid, sa pagpira-piraso ng tinapay, at sa pananalangin. <sup>43</sup> Namangha ang lahat sa maraming himala at tanda na ginawa sa pamamagitan ng mga apostol. <sup>44</sup> Magkakasama ang lahat ng sumasampalataya at ibinabahagi nila ang anumang mayroon sila. <sup>45</sup> Ipinagbibili nila ang kanilang mga ari-arian at ipinamamahagi ang napagbentahan sa sinumang nangangailangan. <sup>46</sup> Araw-araw silang nagtitipon sa templo at nagsasalo-salo sa kanilang mga tahanan nang may galak at bukas na puso. <sup>47</sup> Pinupuri nila ang Diyos at kinalulugdan sila ng lahat. At araw-araw ay idinaragdag ng Panginoon sa kanila ang mga inililigtas.',
  heroCitation: 'Gawa 2:42–47 · salin para sa study',
  themeLabel: 'Tema',
  theme: 'Mapuspos ng Banal na Espiritu. Magkaisa at magmahalan. Ipahayag si Cristo.',
  keyTextsLabel: 'Mga susing talata',
  keyTexts: 'Gawa 2:1–47<br />Juan 15:4<br />Juan 13:34–35<br />Kawikaan 12:1',
  timeLabel: 'Oras',
  time: '30–35 minuto',
  keyVerse: 'Susing talata · salin para sa study',
  presentationLabel: 'Presentation',
  presentationLink: 'Buksan sa Canva <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>',
  serviceLabel: 'Sunday service',
  serviceLink: 'Panoorin sa YouTube <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>',
  section01: '01 · Magsimula rito',
  openingTitle: 'Ang simbahan ay hindi ang gusali—tayo ang simbahan',
  openingLead: 'Ang altar ay hindi lamang isang physical place. Ito ay disposition ng pusong sumusuko sa Diyos. Kaya ang altar ng ating church ay nagsisimula sa tanong: bilang people of God, namumuhay ba tayo ayon sa nais Niya?',
  openingBody: 'Maaaring alisin ang microphone, instruments, ilaw, at mismong building, pero hindi nawawala ang church. Ang church ay ang pagtitipon ng mga taong tinawag ng Diyos at ginawang Kanyang sarili. Sa bahay man, life group, o Sunday gathering, tayo ang iglesya—at binibigyan tayo ng Acts 2 ng larawan kung paano tayo dapat mamuhay.',
  keyTruthLabel: 'Susing katotohanan',
  keyTruth: 'Hindi program, lugar, o kagamitan ang sentro ng church. Si Jesus ang Panginoon, at tayo ang mga taong sama-samang sumusuko sa Kanya.',
  section02: '02 · Alalahanin kung paano isinilang ang church',
  birthTitle: 'Dumating ang Espiritu, ipinahayag si Cristo, at tumugon ang mga tao',
  birthBody1: 'Sa Pentecost, magkakasama ang mga alagad nang dumating sa kanila ang Banal na Espiritu. May tunog na parang malakas na hangin at mga tila-dilang apoy. Nagsalita sila sa iba’t ibang wika ayon sa ibinigay ng Espiritu—at ang narinig ng mga tao ay ang makapangyarihang mga gawa ng Diyos.',
  birthBody2: 'Ipinahayag si Cristo. Ang mga nakarinig ay “cut to the heart”: nakita nila ang kanilang kasalanan at pangangailangan kay Jesus. Nang itanong nila kung ano ang dapat gawin, sinabi ni Pedro na magsisi at magpabautismo. Nang araw ding iyon, humigit-kumulang tatlong libo ang tumugon at nadagdag sa church.',
  birthBody3: 'Hindi nagsimula ang church sa magandang building o mahusay na program. Nagsimula ito sa pagkilos ng Diyos, sa kapangyarihan ng Banal na Espiritu, sa pagpapahayag kay Cristo, at sa mga taong tumugon nang may pananampalataya at pagsunod.',
  discuss1Label: 'Pag-usapan · 1',
  discuss1: 'Kapag naiisip mo ang “church,” ano ang una mong nakikita—building, Sunday program, o people transformed by Jesus? Paano kailangang magbago ang iyong pananaw?',
  section03: '03 · Mapuspos ng Banal na Espiritu',
  spiritTitle: 'Ang puspos na church ay church na binabago',
  spiritBody1: 'Nang dumating ang Banal na Espiritu, nabago ang mga alagad. Hindi lamang sila nagkaroon ng isang spiritual experience; nagbago ang kanilang allegiance. Hindi na sarili, kultura, o dating gawi ang kanilang panginoon. Si Jesus na ang sinusunod nila.',
  spiritBody2: 'Makikita ang pagbabagong ito sa ordinaryong buhay. Ang dating nandaraya, nagsisinungaling, nagmumura, o nananakit ay natututong tumalikod sa lumang paraan dahil nais na niyang malaman at sundin ang kalooban ng Diyos. Kaya tayo nakikinig sa Salita, nananalangin, at nagtitipon: gusto nating manatili kay Cristo.',
  spiritBody3: 'Ang pagiging puspos ng Espiritu ay hindi shortcut sa maturity. Ito ay patuloy na pagsuko at pananatili kay Jesus. Tulad ng sanga na walang bunga kapag hiwalay sa puno, hindi tayo magiging church na ninanais ng Diyos kung hindi tayo nananatili sa Kanya.',
  johnVerse: '<sup>4</sup> “Manatili kayo sa akin, at mananatili ako sa inyo. Kung paanong hindi makapamumunga ang sanga nang mag-isa malibang manatili ito sa puno, hindi rin kayo makapamumunga malibang manatili kayo sa akin.”',
  johnCitation: 'Juan 15:4 · salin para sa study',
  discuss2Label: 'Pag-usapan · 2',
  discuss2: 'Anong lumang ugali o self-rule ang ipinapasuko sa iyo ng Banal na Espiritu? Anong daily practice ang tutulong sa iyong manatili kay Jesus?',
  section04: '04 · Maging devoted araw-araw',
  devotionTitle: 'Teaching. Fellowship. Breaking bread. Prayer.',
  devotionBody1: 'Ang unang believers ay devoted sa turo ng mga apostol, fellowship, breaking of bread, at prayers. Hindi passive attendance ang devotion. Ito ay kusang paglalaan ng puso, oras, at buhay para makilala si Jesus at mamuhay kasama ng Kanyang people.',
  devotionBody2: 'Kapansin-pansin ang salitang “day by day.” Ang church ay hindi lamang event tuwing Sunday. Ang faith ay nabubuhay sa araw-araw—sa pag-aaral ng Salita, pananalangin, pagkain sa iisang hapag, pagbubukas ng tahanan, pag-encourage, at pagsamba nang may galak at generosity.',
  devotionBody3: 'Mahalaga ang programs, life groups, at ministries, pero hindi sila ang pinagmumulan ng buhay. Habang nananatili at sumusunod ang church sa Banal na Espiritu, ang Panginoon ang gumagawa. Ang growth at numbers ay resulta, hindi sentro.',
  discuss3Label: 'Pag-usapan · 3',
  discuss3: 'Alin sa apat—Word, fellowship, shared table, at prayer—ang kailangan mong bigyan ng mas tapat na lugar sa iyong linggo?',
  section05: '05 · Magkaisa at magbahaginan',
  unityTitle: 'Ang pag-ibig ay nagiging practical help',
  unityBody1: 'Ang mga mananampalataya ay magkakasama at may mga bagay na itinuturing nilang para sa kabutihan ng lahat. Ipinagbibili nila ang kanilang possessions at namamahagi ayon sa pangangailangan. Hindi ito performance ng generosity; ito ay pusong nakakakita ng kapatid at tumutugon.',
  unityBody2: 'May mga kapatid na apektado ng baha, may karamdaman, may hospital bills, o nangangailangan ng pagkain at oras. Kung kaya nating tumulong, iunat natin ang ating kamay. Maaari tayong magbigay, bumisita, makinig, magdala ng masarap na pagkain, o manalangin kasama nila. Ang tunay na malasakit ay hindi lamang nagsasabing “I will pray”; kumikilos ito kung may kakayahan.',
  unityBody3: 'Unity is not sameness. Ito ay shared life under one Lord. Kapag ang pangangailangan ng isang kapatid ay nagiging concern ng buong family, nakikita ang altar ng church—mga taong inilalagay ang sarili at resources sa paanan ni Jesus.',
  discuss4Label: 'Pag-usapan · 4',
  discuss4: 'Sino sa church family ang may pangangailangang kaya mong tugunan ngayon—sa oras, pagkain, encouragement, presence, prayer, o financial help?',
  section06: '06 · Magmahal gaya ni Jesus',
  loveTitle: 'Ang paraan ng ating pagmamahalan ay testimony sa mundo',
  loveBody1: 'Binigyan tayo ni Jesus ng bagong command: mahalin ang isa’t isa kung paanong minahal Niya tayo. Hindi optional ang church love. Sa paraan ng ating pakikitungo sa isa’t isa, makikilala ng mundo na tayo ay Kanyang disciples.',
  loveBody2: 'Nasasaktan at nagkakamali tayo dahil walang perfect sa church. Kaya kasama sa pag-ibig ang forgiveness. Hindi credible ang witness natin kung nakangiti tayo sa harap ng kapatid pero sinisiraan siya pagtalikod. Ang altar ng church ay lugar ng grace, truth, repentance, at restored relationships.',
  loveBody3: 'Kasama rin sa love ang humble correction. Maaaring masakit ang saway mula sa magulang, anak, leader, member, kaibigan, o boss, pero ang pusong marunong magpasakop sa Diyos ay handang suriin ang sarili. Ang pagtanggap ng godly discipline ay daan ng karunungan.',
  loveVerse: '<sup>34</sup> “Isang bagong utos ang ibinibigay ko sa inyo: magmahalan kayo. Kung paanong minahal ko kayo, magmahalan din kayo. <sup>35</sup> Sa pamamagitan nito malalaman ng lahat na kayo ay aking mga alagad, kung may pag-ibig kayo sa isa’t isa.”',
  loveCitation: 'Juan 13:34–35 · salin para sa study',
  discuss5Label: 'Pag-usapan · 5',
  discuss5: 'May kapatid ka bang kailangang patawarin, lapitan, tulungan, o pakinggan? May correction ka bang kailangang tanggapin nang may humility?',
  section07: '07 · Ipahayag ang gospel',
  gospelTitle: 'Hindi ito panahon para manatiling tahimik',
  gospelBody1: 'Nang mapuspos ng Espiritu ang mga alagad, ipinahayag nila ang makapangyarihang gawa ng Diyos. Nagsalita si Pedro tungkol kay Jesus; ang mga tao ay naantig, nagsisi, nagpabautismo, at nadagdag sa church. Ang Spirit-filled church ay speaking church.',
  gospelBody2: 'Hindi kailangang nabasa mo na ang buong Bible o nakapagtapos sa seminary bago makapagbahagi. Kailangan mo si Jesus at ang buhay na Kanyang binago. Sabihin sa kapitbahay, kaibigan, kaklase, katrabaho, at kapamilya kung sino Siya at kung ano ang ginawa Niya.',
  gospelBody3: 'Hindi program o ganda ng building ang nagligtas at nagdagdag sa unang church. Ang Panginoon ang gumawa habang ang Kanyang people ay puspos, sumusunod, at nagsasalita. Tayo ang faithful witnesses; sa Diyos ang resulta.',
  discuss6Label: 'Pag-usapan · 6',
  discuss6: 'Sino ang isang taong mapagsasabihan mo tungkol sa kabutihan ni Jesus ngayong linggo? Ano ang maikli at honest na bahagi ng testimony mo na maaari mong ibahagi?',
  section08: '08 · Tumugon',
  responseTitle: 'Maging church na ninanais ng Diyos',
  responseBody1: 'Ang Acts 2 church ay hindi nostalgic picture na hahangaan lang. Ito ang model na tinatawag tayong isabuhay. Isuko natin muli ang altar ng ating church kay Jesus—ang ating mga puso, relationships, resources, conversations, at mission.',
  responseBody2: 'Hindi natin kayang gawin ito sa sariling lakas. Mananatili tayo kay Cristo, magpapasakop sa Banal na Espiritu, at sabay-sabay na susunod sa mga simpleng hakbang ng faithfulness.',
  responseStepLabel: 'Tumugon',
  responseFilled: 'Magpasakop sa Banal na Espiritu at talikuran ang lumang paraan.',
  responseDevoted: 'Maglaan ng araw-araw na oras para sa Word, prayer, at fellowship.',
  responseLove: 'Tulungan, patawarin, at pakinggan ang isang kapatid.',
  responseProclaim: 'Gamitin ang iyong mga salita para ibahagi ang good news of Jesus.',
  declarationLabel: 'Ang ating deklarasyon',
  declaration: '“Tayo ang church. Mananatili tayo kay Jesus, mapupuspos ng Kanyang Espiritu, magmamahalan, at ipapahayag si Cristo. Panginoon, gawin Mo kaming iglesyang ninanais Mo.”',
  section09: '09 · Manalangin',
  prayerTitle: 'Panalangin para sa altar ng ating church',
  prayer1: 'Panginoong Jesus, salamat dahil tinawag Mo kami mula sa kadiliman at ginawa Mo kaming Iyong people. Isinusuko namin sa Iyo ang altar ng aming church. Ikaw ang maging sentro, Panginoon, hindi ang aming programs, building, o sariling kagustuhan.',
  prayer2: 'Puspusin Mo kami ng Banal na Espiritu. Bigyan Mo kami ng gutom sa Iyong Salita, katapatan sa prayer, galak sa fellowship, at pusong bukas sa pagbabago. Turuan Mo kaming manatili sa Iyo araw-araw.',
  prayer3: 'Gawin Mo kaming united church na tumutulong, nagpapatawad, at tumatanggap ng pagtatama nang may humility. Bigyan Mo kami ng tapang na gamitin ang aming mga salita para ipahayag ang kabutihan ni Jesus. Hanggang sa Iyong pagbabalik, matagpuan Mo sana kaming nagmamahalan at tapat sa mission. In Jesus’ name, Amen.',
  takeawayLabel: 'Dalhin mo ito',
  takeaway: 'Be filled. Love one another. Proclaim Christ. Ang church na ninanais ng Diyos ay people who remain in Jesus and live His life together—day by day.',
  shareLabel: 'I-share ang study',
  shareTitle: 'Buksan sa ibang device',
  shareBody: 'I-scan o i-download ang QR code para makabalik diretso sa Bible study na ito.',
  downloadQr: 'I-download ang QR code',
  scriptureNotice: 'Ang mga sipi sa Tagalog ay malayang salin para sa Bible study na ito.',
  footerTagline: 'Sama-samang nakasentro kay Jesus. Hinuhubog ng Kanyang Salita.'
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Altar of Our Church: The Church That God Desires | DMI Calamba City"
  description="A Bible study from Acts 2:42–47 about becoming a Spirit-filled church united in love and faithful to proclaim Christ."
  bodyClass="study-page"
>
  <header class="study-hero">
    <nav class="study-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation" data-i18n-aria-label="navAria">
      <a class="brand-lockup" href={base} aria-label="Return to DMI Calamba City home" data-i18n-aria-label="homeAria">
        <img src={logoPath} width="900" height="900" alt="" />
        <span>DMI · Calamba City</span>
      </a>
      <LanguageToggle translations={translations} />
      <span>06 September 2026</span>
    </nav>

    <div class="study-hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="eyebrow">Bible Study · Acts 2:42–47</p>
      <h1 data-i18n="title">The Altar of Our Church</h1>
      <p class="study-subtitle" data-i18n="subtitle">The Church That God Desires</p>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="hero-scripture">
      <p lang="en" data-i18n="heroScripture" data-i18n-lang><sup>42</sup> And they devoted themselves to the apostles’ teaching and the fellowship, to the breaking of bread and the prayers. <sup>43</sup> And awe came upon every soul, and many wonders and signs were being done through the apostles. <sup>44</sup> And all who believed were together and had all things in common. <sup>45</sup> And they were selling their possessions and belongings and distributing the proceeds to all, as any had need. <sup>46</sup> And day by day, attending the temple together and breaking bread in their homes, they received their food with glad and generous hearts, <sup>47</sup> praising God and having favor with all the people. And the Lord added to their number day by day those who were being saved.</p>
      <cite lang="en" data-i18n="heroCitation" data-i18n-lang>Acts 2:42–47 · ESV</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </header>

  <main class="study-content">
    <aside class="study-aside" aria-label="Study summary" data-i18n-aria-label="summaryAria">
      <div><span class="aside-label" data-i18n="themeLabel">Theme</span><p data-i18n="theme">Be filled with the Holy Spirit. Be united and love one another. Proclaim Christ.</p></div>
      <div><span class="aside-label" data-i18n="keyTextsLabel">Key texts</span><p data-i18n="keyTexts">Acts 2:1–47<br />John 15:4<br />John 13:34–35<br />Proverbs 12:1</p></div>
      <div><span class="aside-label" data-i18n="timeLabel">Time</span><p data-i18n="time">30–35 minutes</p></div>
      <div><span class="aside-label" data-i18n="presentationLabel">Presentation</span><a class="aside-action" href="https://www.canva.com/design/DAHUXr_nCu0/_6U-DsT_u8WPZzo2aAYlfg/edit" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-i18n="presentationLink">Open in Canva <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div><span class="aside-label" data-i18n="serviceLabel">Sunday service</span><a class="aside-action" href="https://www.youtube.com/live/iANRJKYjYxM" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-i18n="serviceLink">Watch on YouTube <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </aside>

    <article class="study-article">
      <section class="opening" aria-labelledby="opening-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section01">01 · Begin here</p>
        <h2 id="opening-title" data-i18n="openingTitle">The church is not the building—we are the church</h2>
        <p class="lead" data-i18n="openingLead">An altar is not merely a physical place. It is the disposition of a heart surrendered to God. So the altar of our church begins with a question: as God’s people, are we living the way he intends?</p>
        <p data-i18n="openingBody">Remove the microphone, instruments, lights, and even the building, and the church remains. The church is the assembly of people God has called and made his own. Whether in a home, a life group, or a Sunday gathering, we are the church—and Acts 2 gives us a picture of how we should live.</p>
        <div class="key-statement"><span data-i18n="keyTruthLabel">Key truth</span><p data-i18n="keyTruth">A program, place, or equipment is not the center of the church. Jesus is Lord, and we are a people surrendered to him together.</p></div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="birth-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section02">02 · Remember how the church was born</p>
        <h2 id="birth-title" data-i18n="birthTitle">The Spirit came, Christ was proclaimed, and people responded</h2>
        <p data-i18n="birthBody1">At Pentecost, the disciples were together when the Holy Spirit came upon them. There was a sound like a mighty rushing wind and what appeared to be tongues of fire. They spoke in different languages as the Spirit enabled them—and people heard the mighty works of God.</p>
        <p data-i18n="birthBody2">Christ was proclaimed. Those listening were “cut to the heart”: they saw their sin and their need for Jesus. When they asked what to do, Peter told them to repent and be baptized. About three thousand responded that same day and were added to the church.</p>
        <p data-i18n="birthBody3">The church did not begin with a beautiful building or polished program. It began with God’s action, the Holy Spirit’s power, the proclamation of Christ, and people responding in faith and obedience.</p>
        <div class="discussion-prompt"><span data-i18n="discuss1Label">Discuss · 1</span><p data-i18n="discuss1">When you think of “church,” what comes to mind first—a building, a Sunday program, or people transformed by Jesus? How must your perspective change?</p></div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="spirit-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section03">03 · Be filled with the Holy Spirit</p>
        <h2 id="spirit-title" data-i18n="spiritTitle">A Spirit-filled church is a transformed church</h2>
        <p data-i18n="spiritBody1">When the Holy Spirit came, the disciples changed. They did not merely have a spiritual experience; their allegiance changed. Self, culture, and former habits were no longer lord. They now followed Jesus.</p>
        <p data-i18n="spiritBody2">This transformation appears in ordinary life. Someone who once cheated, lied, cursed, or harmed others learns to turn from the old way because they now want to know and obey God’s will. This is why we listen to the Word, pray, and gather: we want to remain in Christ.</p>
        <p data-i18n="spiritBody3">Being filled with the Spirit is not a shortcut to maturity. It is continuing surrender and abiding in Jesus. As a branch cannot bear fruit apart from the vine, we cannot become the church God desires unless we remain in him.</p>
        <blockquote class="verse-card"><span data-i18n="keyVerse">Key verse · study translation</span><p lang="en" data-i18n="johnVerse" data-i18n-lang><sup>4</sup> “Abide in me, and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit by itself, unless it abides in the vine, neither can you, unless you abide in me.”</p><cite lang="en" data-i18n="johnCitation" data-i18n-lang>John 15:4 · ESV</cite></blockquote>
        <div class="discussion-prompt"><span data-i18n="discuss2Label">Discuss · 2</span><p data-i18n="discuss2">What old habit or self-rule is the Holy Spirit asking you to surrender? What daily practice will help you remain in Jesus?</p></div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="devotion-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section04">04 · Be devoted day by day</p>
        <h2 id="devotion-title" data-i18n="devotionTitle">Teaching. Fellowship. Breaking bread. Prayer.</h2>
        <p data-i18n="devotionBody1">The first believers devoted themselves to the apostles’ teaching, fellowship, breaking bread, and prayers. Devotion is not passive attendance. It is willingly giving our hearts, time, and lives to know Jesus and live with his people.</p>
        <p data-i18n="devotionBody2">Notice the words “day by day.” Church is not only a Sunday event. Faith lives daily—in Scripture, prayer, meals around one table, open homes, encouragement, and worship with glad and generous hearts.</p>
        <p data-i18n="devotionBody3">Programs, life groups, and ministries matter, but they are not the source of life. As the church abides and follows the Holy Spirit, the Lord works. Growth and numbers are a result, not the center.</p>
        <div class="discussion-prompt"><span data-i18n="discuss3Label">Discuss · 3</span><p data-i18n="discuss3">Which of the four—Word, fellowship, shared table, and prayer—needs a more faithful place in your week?</p></div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="unity-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section05">05 · Be united and share</p>
        <h2 id="unity-title" data-i18n="unityTitle">Love becomes practical help</h2>
        <p data-i18n="unityBody1">The believers were together and held what they had for the good of all. They sold possessions and distributed the proceeds according to need. This was not performative generosity; it was a heart that noticed a brother or sister and responded.</p>
        <p data-i18n="unityBody2">Some in the church may be affected by flooding, illness, hospital bills, food shortages, or loneliness. If we can help, let us extend our hands. We can give, visit, listen, bring good food, or pray with them. Genuine care does not only say, “I will pray”; it acts when it has the ability.</p>
        <p data-i18n="unityBody3">Unity is not sameness. It is shared life under one Lord. When one person’s need becomes the concern of the whole family, the church’s altar becomes visible—people placing themselves and their resources at Jesus’ feet.</p>
        <div class="discussion-prompt"><span data-i18n="discuss4Label">Discuss · 4</span><p data-i18n="discuss4">Who in the church family has a need you can meet today—with time, food, encouragement, presence, prayer, or financial help?</p></div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="love-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section06">06 · Love as Jesus loved</p>
        <h2 id="love-title" data-i18n="loveTitle">The way we love one another is a testimony to the world</h2>
        <p data-i18n="loveBody1">Jesus gave us a new command: love one another as he loved us. Love within the church is not optional. By the way we treat one another, the world will recognize that we are his disciples.</p>
        <p data-i18n="loveBody2">We hurt and fail one another because no one in the church is perfect. Therefore, love includes forgiveness. Our witness is not credible if we smile at someone face-to-face and tear them down when they turn away. The church’s altar is a place of grace, truth, repentance, and restored relationships.</p>
        <p data-i18n="loveBody3">Love also includes humble correction. Reproof from a parent, child, leader, member, friend, or boss may hurt, but a heart submitted to God is willing to examine itself. Receiving godly discipline is the path of wisdom.</p>
        <blockquote class="verse-card"><span data-i18n="keyVerse">Key verse · study translation</span><p lang="en" data-i18n="loveVerse" data-i18n-lang><sup>34</sup> “A new commandment I give to you, that you love one another: just as I have loved you, you also are to love one another. <sup>35</sup> By this all people will know that you are my disciples, if you have love for one another.”</p><cite lang="en" data-i18n="loveCitation" data-i18n-lang>John 13:34–35 · ESV</cite></blockquote>
        <div class="discussion-prompt"><span data-i18n="discuss5Label">Discuss · 5</span><p data-i18n="discuss5">Is there someone you need to forgive, approach, help, or listen to? Is there correction you need to receive with humility?</p></div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="gospel-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section07">07 · Proclaim the gospel</p>
        <h2 id="gospel-title" data-i18n="gospelTitle">This is not the time to remain silent</h2>
        <p data-i18n="gospelBody1">When the disciples were filled with the Spirit, they proclaimed God’s mighty works. Peter spoke about Jesus; people were convicted, repented, were baptized, and joined the church. A Spirit-filled church is a speaking church.</p>
        <p data-i18n="gospelBody2">You do not need to have read the whole Bible or graduated from seminary before you can share. You need Jesus and the life he has transformed. Tell a neighbor, friend, classmate, coworker, or family member who he is and what he has done.</p>
        <p data-i18n="gospelBody3">A program or beautiful building did not save people and add them to the first church. The Lord worked as his people were filled, obedient, and vocal. We are faithful witnesses; the result belongs to God.</p>
        <div class="discussion-prompt"><span data-i18n="discuss6Label">Discuss · 6</span><p data-i18n="discuss6">Who is one person you can tell about the goodness of Jesus this week? What brief, honest part of your testimony can you share?</p></div>
      </section>

      <section class="response-section" aria-labelledby="response-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section08">08 · Respond</p>
        <h2 id="response-title" data-i18n="responseTitle">Become the church God desires</h2>
        <p data-i18n="responseBody1">The Acts 2 church is not a nostalgic picture to admire. It is a model we are called to live. Let us surrender the altar of our church again to Jesus—our hearts, relationships, resources, conversations, and mission.</p>
        <p data-i18n="responseBody2">We cannot do this in our own strength. We will remain in Christ, submit to the Holy Spirit, and take simple steps of faithfulness together.</p>
        <ol class="response-steps">
          <li><span data-i18n="responseStepLabel">Respond</span><p data-i18n="responseFilled">Submit to the Holy Spirit and turn from the old way.</p></li>
          <li><span data-i18n="responseStepLabel">Respond</span><p data-i18n="responseDevoted">Make daily room for the Word, prayer, and fellowship.</p></li>
          <li><span data-i18n="responseStepLabel">Respond</span><p data-i18n="responseLove">Help, forgive, and listen to a brother or sister.</p></li>
          <li><span data-i18n="responseStepLabel">Respond</span><p data-i18n="responseProclaim">Use your words to share the good news of Jesus.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="key-statement dark"><span data-i18n="declarationLabel">Our declaration</span><p data-i18n="declaration">“We are the church. We will remain in Jesus, be filled with his Spirit, love one another, and proclaim Christ. Lord, make us the church you desire.”</p></div>
      </section>

      <section class="closing-prayer" aria-labelledby="prayer-title">
        <p class="section-number" data-i18n="section09">09 · Pray</p>
        <h2 id="prayer-title" data-i18n="prayerTitle">A prayer for the altar of our church</h2>
        <p data-i18n="prayer1">Lord Jesus, thank You for calling us out of darkness and making us Your people. We surrender the altar of our church to You. Be our center, Lord—not our programs, building, or personal preferences.</p>
        <p data-i18n="prayer2">Fill us with the Holy Spirit. Give us hunger for Your Word, faithfulness in prayer, joy in fellowship, and hearts open to transformation. Teach us to remain in You day by day.</p>
        <p data-i18n="prayer3">Make us a united church that helps, forgives, and receives correction with humility. Give us courage to use our words to proclaim the goodness of Jesus. Until You return, may You find us loving one another and faithful to the mission. In Jesus’ name, Amen.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="takeaway" aria-label="Study takeaway" data-i18n-aria-label="takeawayAria"><span data-i18n="takeawayLabel">Take this with you</span><p data-i18n="takeaway">Be filled. Love one another. Proclaim Christ. The church God desires is a people who remain in Jesus and live his life together—day by day.</p></section>

